                <pb facs="0295" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860d.01/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-19T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>792. Is Department correct in assuming that you will answer direct Stockholm
                    Legation’s telegram No. 100, February 15 to you regarding recognition of
                    Finland?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
